The ping-pong latency benchmark on the machine's GPU, on few rounds: node
1's target region against node 2 over TCP and against its echo thread,
and the RPC floor's region.
REQUIRES: amdgpu-gpu

RUN: merkc -O2 -fopenmp --offload-arch=%offload-arch %libomp-flags %S/../../benchmarks/pingpong/pingpong.m -o %t
RUN: %libomp-env OMP_TARGET_OFFLOAD=MANDATORY %python %S/../../benchmarks/pingpong/pair.py %t gpu 200 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=GPU
RUN: %libomp-env OMP_TARGET_OFFLOAD=MANDATORY %t gpu-local 200 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=GPU-LOCAL
RUN: clang++ -O2 -std=c++17 -fopenmp --offload-arch=%offload-arch -I%S/../../../libc %libomp-flags %S/../../benchmarks/pingpong/rpc-floor.cpp -o %t.rpc
RUN: %libomp-env OMP_TARGET_OFFLOAD=MANDATORY %t.rpc 200 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=RPC
GPU: gpu {{ *}}200 rounds, {{ *}}200 in order, {{.*}} us a round
GPU-NEXT: launch {{.*}} us
GPU-LOCAL: gpu-local {{ *}}200 rounds, {{ *}}200 in order, {{.*}} us a round
RPC: rpc-floor {{ *}}200 rounds, {{ *}}200 in order, {{.*}} us a round
RPC-NEXT: launch {{.*}} us
